{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1790347384,"nonce":"/dudOnqv1G89uLsx8xd9kZ3wgV8=","target":"f2f81ae4948255d713978458ee40e00308d552d42087f8a66e21d8a5505ed47e","message":"A language server for ZynML: diagnostics as the file is edited, hover with the inferred type, go-to-definition and find-references across imported modules, and completion for locals, struct fields, impl methods and stdlib names. It ships with the VS Code extension that today holds only the TextMate grammar (.vscode/extensions/zynml-syntax).\n\nThe server runs the ZynML front half (zyn_peg parse, typed AST, type checking) and stops before lowering. What it builds on:\n- Spans carry their file (typed_ast diagnostics.rs), so a diagnostic can point into an imported module.\n- Typed diagnostics (f7eab5774f0ef8d5db37921713c2b14f13beda99a906c167ee01ae47b0e96eb7) give the server diagnostic kinds instead of strings, so it can map each to an LSP severity and range.\n- The typed AST keeps a type per expression, which hover and completion read.\n\nOwed before it is usable on real files: parse recovery so one syntax error does not blank the file, and a symbol index per module so references resolve without re-checking every import on each keystroke.\n\nThis is ZynML only; zypy and zylua use the ecosystem's Python and Lua language servers.","files":null}]}